          "author": {
            "email": "alx@kernel.org",
            "name": "Alejandro Colomar"
          },
          "message": "lib/string/sprintf/: [v]asprintf_(): Add functions\n\nThese functions are just like [v]asprintf(3), but simpler.\n\nThey return the newly allocated memory, which allows us to use the\n[[gnu::malloc(free)]] attribute, which enhances static analysis.\nThey also omit the length, which we don't care about at all.\n\nSigned-off-by: Alejandro Colomar <alx@kernel.org>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/alejandro-colomar/shadow/commits/0208335f5f5f77cb54c647fe681d968a50726fd6"
        },
        {
          "sha": "bded46ce38682a1e3e3f52dddde788987f5b3a2e",
          "author": {
            "email": "alx@kernel.org",
            "name": "Alejandro Colomar"
          },
          "message": "lib/tcbfuncs.c: Split conditionals\n\nThis is in preparation for the next commit.\n\nSigned-off-by: Alejandro Colomar <alx@kernel.org>",
          "distinct": true,
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/alejandro-colomar/shadow/commits/bded46ce38682a1e3e3f52dddde788987f5b3a2e"
        },
        {
