        "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "# Refactor FriendsController: Remove Unnecessary Endpoints and Add 'Get Friends' Endpoint\r\n\r\n## Description\r\nRefactor the `FriendsController` by removing unused or redundant endpoints and introducing a new `GET /friends` endpoint. This endpoint will allow the retrieval of the current user's friends.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance Criteria\r\n- **Removal of Unnecessary Endpoints:**\r\n  - Identify and remove any endpoints within the `FriendsController` that are no longer used or relevant to the application's functionality.\r\n  - Ensure removed endpoints are documented for reference and communicated to the team.\r\n\r\n- **Addition of `GET /friends` Endpoint:**\r\n  - Add a new `GET /friends` endpoint in the `FriendsController`.\r\n  - Endpoint should:\r\n    - Authenticate the current user.\r\n    - Retrieve and return the list of friends associated with the current user.\r\n    - Return JSON response with the following structure:\r\n      ```json\r\n      {\r\n        \"friends\": [\r\n          {\r\n            \"id\": \"123\",\r\n            \"name\": \"John Doe\",\r\n            \"profile_picture\": \"url_to_picture\"\r\n          },\r\n          ...\r\n        ]\r\n      }\r\n      ```\r\n  - Handle common errors:\r\n    - 401 if the user is not authenticated.\r\n    - 500 for unexpected issues.\r\n\r\n## Technical Considerations\r\n- Ensure the `GET /friends` endpoint leverages existing services or repositories to fetch friends efficiently.\r\n- Remove unused methods in the `FriendsController` and related services if they are tied to the removed endpoints.\r\n- Apply pagination to the `GET /friends` response if the number of friends is significant.\r\n- Update Swagger or API documentation to reflect the changes in the `FriendsController`.\r\n\r\n## Definition of Done\r\n- All unused endpoints and methods in `FriendsController` are removed.\r\n- The new `GET /friends` endpoint is implemented and documented.\r\n- The functionality is verified in the staging environment.\r\n- All code changes are reviewed and approved by the team.\r\n- Updated API documentation is shared with relevant stakeholders.\r\n",
