        "body": "### Describe the Issue\n\nStep 20 in learn-basic-css-by-building-a-cafe-menu\n\nThe instructions say:\n> Add a div element inside the body element and then move all the other elements inside the new div.\n> Inside the opening div tag, add the id attribute with a value of menu.\n\n### Affected Page\n\nhttps://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/2022/responsive-web-design/learn-basic-css-by-building-a-cafe-menu/step-20\n\n### Your code\n\n```\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>Cafe Menu</title>\n    <link href=\"styles.css\" rel=\"stylesheet\"/>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <main>\n      <h1>CAMPER CAFE</h1>\n      <p>Est. 2020</p>\n      <section>\n        <h2>Coffee</h2>\n      </section>\n    </main>\n    <div id=\"menu\">\n    </div>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nTest should fail, because the instruction says \"move all the other elements inside the new div\".\n\nStep 21 has the following HTML:\n\n```\n    <div id=\"menu\">\n      <main>\n        <h1>CAMPER CAFE</h1>\n        <p>Est. 2020</p>\n        <section>\n          <h2>Coffee</h2>\n        </section>\n      </main>\n    </div>\n```\n\n### Screenshots\n\n<img width=\"727\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/018922b7-d7f1-4dd4-978c-d063056c09e1\" />\n\n\n### System\n\n- Device: MacBook Air\n- OS: macOS Sonoma 14.5\n- Browser: Brave [Version 1.73.104 Chromium: 131.0.6778.204 (Official Build) (arm64)](https://brave.com/latest/)\n- Version: 1.73.104\n\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
